<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Micind reverses tourism into M&amp;A.</title>
<headline>Micind reverses tourism into M&amp;A.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Micor Industrial Corp said on Monday it had disposed of its tourism and travel interests to new company Tourvest which would be reversed into the cash shell of Mathieson and Ashley Holdings Ltd.</p>
<p>Following the move, M&amp;A's listing will be terminated and Tourvest will be listed on the Beverages, Hotels and Leisure sector.</p>
<p>Tourvest has a net asset and trade mark value of 35.69 million rand.</p>
<p>Micind also said it was in unrelated talks which could have an impact on its share price and urged shareholders to exercise caution in their dealings.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
